594	//! The regions a layer's picture carries — [`Spotlight`],
595	//! [`ObscureRegion`], the [`SpotShape`] both are drawn with and the
596	//! [`MAX_OBSCURE`] budget on the second (spec §4.2, §5.2).
597	//!
598	//! Split out of `model_props.rs` under the size rule (core/CLAUDE.md: a
599	//! module over ~600 lines gives something up before it takes anything on)
600	//! when road map 2's phase 3c added `video.obscure` and pushed it over.
601	//! `model.rs` → `model_query.rs` in phase 0, and `model.rs` →
602	//! `model_props.rs` in phase 2, are the precedent, and so is their rule:
603	//! the cut goes along a seam somebody can NAME, and the piece taken out is
604	//! re-exported whole so not one path anywhere else changes.
605	//!
606	//! # The seam: one frame, one shape
607	//!
608	//! These are not three property types that happened to be adjacent. A
609	//! region is a box drawn ON the picture, and every box here is in the same
610	//! frame:
611	//!
612	//! > `x` and `y` are the region's CENTRE, as an offset in SOURCE pixels
613	//! > from the centre of the layer's CROPPED rect, y down; `width` and
614	//! > `height` are its size in those same pixels.
615	//!
616	//! Nothing here is in canvas pixels, and nothing here is a fraction of
617	//! anything. That is deliberate and it is the whole reason the frame is
618	//! worth a module of its own: a box in source pixels rides with the layer
619	//! it was drawn on, through `scale`, `x`/`y`, `rotation` and a nest's
620	//! transform, so the region stays on the face — or the password field, or
621	//! the notification — it was put on. A layer's own crop is the only edit
622	//! that moves it, which is why the origin is the CROPPED rect's centre and
623	//! not the source's: crop trims in place (see [`crate::model::Crop`]), so
624	//! measuring from the trimmed centre is what keeps a centred region
625	//! centred. `edit_zoom.rs` calls this frame Q and writes out the equation
626	//! that turns a length in it into canvas pixels; that module doc is the
627	//! canonical derivation and nothing here repeats it.
628	//!
629	//! The second half of the seam is [`SpotShape`]. A region needs a distance
630	//! field to feather against, both of these need the same two — a rectangle
